WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.245
Digital footprints are observable traces created through active sharing, passive collection,

00:00:05.245 --> 00:00:08.520
public records, technical infrastructure, and third-party references.

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:14.601
They can be personal, professional, organizational, or technical, and they change over time.

00:00:14.601 --> 00:00:19.278
Active footprints include posts, profiles, documents, and code intentionally published.

00:00:19.278 --> 00:00:23.488
Passive footprints include logs, indexing, metadata, tracking, data-broker records,

00:00:23.488 --> 00:00:25.359
and reported service exposure.

00:00:25.359 --> 00:00:30.972
One item may be low risk while aggregation reveals sensitive relationships, routines,

00:00:30.972 --> 00:00:31.908
or infrastructure.

00:00:31.908 --> 00:00:36.118
Responsible analysis validates identity, origin, accuracy, timeliness, and context.

00:00:36.118 --> 00:00:41.263
It distinguishes ownership from association and current conditions from historical records.

00:00:41.263 --> 00:00:45.473
Public availability never authorizes harassment, doxxing, impersonation, unauthorized access,

00:00:45.473 --> 00:00:47.812
or misuse of personal information.

00:00:47.812 --> 00:00:52.022
Risk reduction combines account security, privacy settings, careful publishing,

00:00:52.022 --> 00:00:56.700
metadata review, asset ownership, repository and service hygiene, employee awareness,

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.974
and recurring monitoring for legitimate defensive purposes.

00:00:59.974 --> 00:01:03.716
The objective is intentional control, not total disappearance.

00:01:03.716 --> 00:01:10.265
A well-managed footprint supports useful public communication and accountable operations while limiting unnecessary detail.

00:01:10.265 --> 00:01:15.878
Ethical analysis uses proportionality and evidence to reduce privacy and security risk

00:01:15.878 --> 00:01:19.620
without exploiting the people represented by the data.
